"You were born without an account" = "您生来就没有帐户";
"Nobody tracked your conversations. No one drew a map of where you'd been. Privacy was never a feature - it was the way of life." = "没有人追踪您的对话。没有人绘制您去过的地图。隐私从来不是一个功能——它是一种生活方式。";
"Then we moved online, and every platform asked for a piece of you - your name, your number, your friends. We accepted that the price of talking to others is letting someone know who we talk to. Every generation, people and tech, had it this way - telephone, email, messengers, social media. It seemed the only way possible." = "然后我们上线了，每个平台都要求您的一部分 - 您的姓名、您的号码、您的朋友。我们接受了与他人交谈的代价就是让别人知道我们在和谁说话。每一代人，无论是人还是技术，都是这样 - 电话、电子邮件、即时通讯、社交媒体。这似乎是唯一可能的方式。";
"There is another way. A network with no phone numbers. No usernames. No accounts. No user identities of any kind. A network that connects people and carries encrypted messages without knowing who is connected." = "还有另一种方式。一个没有电话号码的网络。没有用户名。没有帐户。没有任何形式的用户身份。一个连接人们并传递加密消息而不知道谁在连接的网络。";
"Not a better lock on someone else's door. Not a nicer landlord that respects your privacy, but still keeps the record of all visitors. You are not a guest. You are home. No king can enter it - you are sovereign." = "不是别人门上更好的锁。不是更尊重您隐私但仍记录所有访客的更好房东。您不是客人。您在家。没有国王能进入——您是主权者。";
"Your conversations belong to you, as it had always been before the Internet. The network is not a place you visit. It is a place you create and own. And nobody can take it from you, whether you make it private or public." = "您的对话属于您，就像互联网出现之前一直如此。网络不是您访问的地方。它是您创建和拥有的地方。没有人能从您那里夺走它，无论您使其私密还是公开。";
"The oldest human freedom - to speak to another person without being watched - built on infrastructure that cannot betray it." = "最古老的人类自由 - 在不被监视的情况下与另一个人交谈 - 建立在无法背叛它的基础设施之上。";
"Because we destroyed the power to know who you are. So that your power can never be taken." = "因为我们摧毁了知道你是谁的力量。这样你的力量就永远不会被夺走。";
